Looking at the current font setup, there are four specific reasons the typography doesn't look like a real private bank yet:
Monospace on dollar amounts (DM Mono): Balances like CAD $1,622,886.00 currently use font-mono, which gives them wide typewriter spacing like a developer console. Real banks render money in their primary sans-serif with tabular-nums (aligned columns, crisp proportions) and reserve monospace strictly for account numbers (•••• 4821), SWIFT/routing codes, and reference IDs (TXN-000142).
Global serif on every heading (h1–h6): Cormorant Garamond is currently forced on every <h2> and <h3> across cards, tables, and modals. Thin editorial serifs look great on a brand wordmark or main greeting, but make card headers (Accounts, Holdings, Transaction history) look spindly instead of crisp and institutional.
Missing 700 bold weight & tight tracking: The stylesheet imports DM Sans only up to weight 600, so font-bold relies on browser-faked bolding, and -0.01em global tracking makes small labels feel slightly cramped.
Font bloat in index.html: index.html currently requests 26 unrelated Google Font families at once (including Architects Daughter, Oxanium, Roboto, Space Grotesk, etc.), slowing initial rendering.
Recommended Typography Options for Modern Private Bank
Option A: Swiss Private Bank (Recommended — UBS / Julius Baer / Coutts feel)
UI, Headings & Tabular Balances: Plus Jakarta Sans (400, 500, 600, 700 + tabular-nums) — crisp, modern private-wealth proportions with very legible currency figures.
Brand Wordmark & Main Greeting only: Cormorant Garamond — preserves Veritas Wealth's heritage feel without cluttering data cards.
Account Numbers & Ref IDs only: IBM Plex Mono — clean institutional monospace strictly for codes and masked numbers.
Option B: Institutional & Tier-1 Bank (HSBC Premier / Morgan Stanley feel)
UI, Headings & Tabular Balances: IBM Plex Sans (400, 500, 600, 700 + tabular-nums) — authoritative, razor-sharp at 12px–14px table sizes and large balances alike.
Brand Wordmark & Main Greeting only: Playfair Display or Cormorant Garamond.
Account Numbers & Ref IDs only: IBM Plex Mono.
Option C: Modern WealthTech (Mercury / Wealthsimple Private feel)
UI, Headings & Tabular Balances: Manrope (400, 500, 600, 700 + tabular-nums) — clean geometric curves and ultra-sharp numerals.
Brand Wordmark & Main Greeting only: Cormorant Garamond.
Account Numbers & Ref IDs only: JetBrains Mono.
